    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "API → x.emails → q.emails.* → emails worker → SMTP",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "\n- **Topology** lives in `HrAgencySystem.EmailTemplates.Messaging`: exchange `x.emails` (topic, vhost `development`), one queue per domain - `q.emails.recruitment`, `identity`, `sales`, `teams`, `agency` - bound by `<domain>.#`.\n- **Healthy**: *Published* ≈ *Consumed*, queues near 0, *Dead letters* 0, *Unroutable* 0, every email queue has consumers.\n- **Backlog**: a queue that grows while *Consumer utilisation* is high → the worker is too slow (SMTP): scale `EmailsWorkerReplicaCount` or ListenerCount. Growing with **no consumers** → the worker is down (*Emails worker* dashboard, *Reporting*).\n- **Outbox growing** in the API while the broker is up → publishing fails; the API logs say why (Rootprint, service `hr-api`).\n- **Dead letters**: inspect in the [RabbitMQ UI](http://localhost:15672) (`wolverine-dead-letter-queue`); the failure with its trace id is in Rootprint logs of `hr-notification-worker`.\n- Traffic: `./infrastructure/start.sh --emails` (password resets → `SendPasswordReset` → `q.emails.identity`).\n"
      },
      "id": 29,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 47
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      }
    }
